 log files, not security- or availability-impacting, but were never cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87d6026b9f564329","cmd-43b92472ddfb42a6","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task's three material outcomes (rootless containerized web app running as appsvc, served on port 8080, and boot-start persistence without a login session) are all satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. Notably, the restart-evidence trace does not merely show configuration: it captures a genuine pre-fix boot-start failure during the first reboot, the diagnosis and fix, and then a clean auto-start on a second independent reboot with a distinct boot identity, HTTP 200 confirmed on loopback and NODE_IP, correct process ownership, and no active login session for appsvc — satisfying the higher evidentiary bar required for boot/restart-related outcomes. Hygiene is generally good; the only issues are a bounded, fully-reverted troubleshooting mutation and some leftover diagnostic log files in /tmp.","limitations":["The captured evidence relies on shell command outputs and does not include independent artifact verification (e.g., contents of the final /etc/init.d/appsvc-webapp file after the fix, beyond what was echoed during the heredoc write and syntax check).","ps output truncates the full conmon command line in several captures, but ownership (appsvc) and the presence of the nginx master process remain clearly legible.","No loginctl/systemd session manager exists on this Alpine node (busybox who/last used instead), a slightly weaker session-absence check than loginctl but standard for this OS and applied consistently across all checks."]},"ttft_ms":23560,"type":"result","duration_ms":72809,"uuid":"f22c9cf0-a4e2-47ef-998a-c2713a1fdb1c","ttft_stream_ms":2619,"time_to_request_ms":197,"first_content_frame_ms":2619,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
